+ * - SMI_LARB_CMD_THRT_CON (0x24) bit 27 is cleared on LARB2 - the camera larb
+ *   - once at boot: smi_configuration.c:1276 in the SMI_D1 branch
+ *   (M4U_ReadReg32(LARB2_BASE, 0x24) & 0xf7ffffff).  The ROM image runs the
+ *   same read-modify-write at smi_set_nonconstant_variable+0x10
+ *   (ldr [r3,#0x24] @0xc04ca99c, bic #0x08000000 @0xc04ca9a4,
+ *   str [r3,#0x24] @0xc04ca9ac).  The bit has no documented name; only the
+ *   position is known, so it is cleared and nothing else is touched.
+ *
+ * - SMI_LARB_OSTDL_PORT (0x200 + 4 * port), the per-port outstanding-request
+ *   limit.  The values come from smi_profile_setting_larb2_init
+ *   (smi_configuration.c:127-134; 21 ports, all 1) and are applied by
+ *   smi_bus_regs_setting() on every "normal" SMI profile (smi_common.c:1255).
+ *   The same table is present in the ROM image (file offset 0xe80ad8,
+ *   virtual 0xc0e849b4) and is written by the ROM's copy of
+ *   smi_bus_regs_setting (word loop @0xc04ca85c-0xc04ca890).
+ *
+ * The larb's own registers are lost when its power domain (ISP for LARB2,
+ * DIS for LARB0, ...) cycles, so the two settings are re-applied together
+ * with the MMU bitmap on every larb resume.
+ *
+ * SMI_LARB_OSTDL_SOFT_EN (0x64) is written by the vendor code as well
+ * (smi_common.c:793), but only from a path that runs while the larb is idle
+ * and with no documented field semantics; mainline configures OSTDL_PORT on
+ * every supported SoC without it, so it is left alone.
